# Documentation Convention

This project has exactly 4 canonical documentation files in `docs/`:

| File | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `docs/README.md` | Product overview, architecture, supported protocols, optional services |
| `docs/LOCAL_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` | Local K3s/Vagrant deployment, all phases, commands |
| `docs/AKS_DEPLOYMENT_GUIDE.md` | AKS/private cluster deployment (stub, to be filled) |
| `docs/TROUBLESHOOTING_GUIDE.md` | Errors, fixes, debugging steps per protocol |

## Rules

- NEVER create a new documentation file unless the user explicitly asks for one.
- NEVER update documentation without first telling the user which of the 4 files above will be updated and asking for confirmation.
- Always say: "This belongs in `docs/X.md` — shall I update it there?" before writing.
- If content could fit in more than one doc, state both options and ask which the user prefers.
- Do NOT add documentation to `deployments/`, `helm-charts/`, or any other folder unless the user explicitly requests it.
